    { 11188, "What's taking her so long?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11188
    { 11200, "Where's Mikhail?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11200
    { 11201, "Filing duty in the main records building." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11201
    { 11202, "Why? What did he do?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11202
    { 11203, "Zhukov caught him with an American magazine." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11203
    { 11204, "Pornography?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11204
    { 11205, "Worse. Investment planning." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11205
    { 11206, "I never would have figured Mikhail for a Capitalist swine." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11206
    { 11207, "He said he was using it for toilet paper because they've been out for three weeks and he didn't want to soil patriotic literature." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11207
    { 11208, "And Zhukov still punished him?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11208
    { 11209, "If you ask me, he just wanted the magazine. He couldn't confiscate it if he didn't punish Mikhail." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11209
    { 11210, "Now that you mention it, Zhukov IS getting close to retirement." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11210
    { 11211, "How do they expect us to stay fit eating this gruel?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11211
    { 11212, "I miss borscht." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11212
    { 11213, "I miss pirogi." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11213
    { 11214, "I miss bread." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11214
    { 11215, "But we HAVE bread." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11215
    { 11216, "I'd rather eat rocks. You can kill a rabbit with this bread." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11216
    { 11217, "Actually, that's not a bad idea." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11217
    { 11218, "Rabbit stew?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11218
    { 11219, "I'm patrolling the west perimeter tomorrow. I'll hunt, you cook." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11219
    { 11220, "It's a deal." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11220
    { 11221, "Have they found out what's wrong with the communications relay?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11221
    { 11222, "I haven't heard." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11222
    { 11223, "Well, stay alert. It might have been sabotage." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11223
    { 11224, "Have you seen Mikhail?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11224
    { 11225, "He was filing documents down the hall." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11225
    { 11226, "He's not there now." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11226
    { 11227, "Maybe he's in the restroom." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11227
    { 11228, "I already checked." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11228
    { 11229, "Smoking a cigarette?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11229
    { 11230, "I searched everywhere. He's just gone." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11230
    { 11231, "He could have gone back to the barracks." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11231
    { 11232, "In the middle of a shift? He's on duty for another 11 hours." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11232
    { 11233, "How could he just vanish?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11233
    { 11234, "Boris vanished last month." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11234
    { 11235, "Boris went AWOL. He must have." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11235
    { 11236, "Without taking his coat? Or his hat?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11236
    { 11237, "This is the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics. People don't just vanish without a trace." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11237
    { 11238, "Tell that to Mikhail." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11238
    { 11239, "You're new here, aren't you." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11239
    { 11240, "I was transferred from Novgorod to work on Project: Omega." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11240
    { 11241, "I've heard of that. What is it, anyway?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11241
    { 11242, "I'm not sure. Nobody told me anything about it. I've spent three days trying to find information." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11242
    { 11243, "Did you check the M-9 mainframe?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11243
    { 11244, "It's out of order. One of the vacuum tubes blew and nobody can find a replacement." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11244
    { 11245, "I saw one in the basement the other day." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11245
    { 11246, "Where?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11246
    { 11247, "I don't remember exactly. Either on a shelf or in a cabinet." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11247
    { 11248, "How much longer do we have to put up with them?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11248
    { 11249, "Until the project's finished." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11249
    { 11250, "How long is that?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11250
    { 11251, "Nobody's sure. I don't think anybody even knows what it is." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11251
    { 11252, "It better be soon. I'm running out of patience." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11252
    { 11253, "I'm sure they're terrified." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11253
    { 11254, "They should be." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11254
    { 11255, "She may try to come this way. Stay alert!" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11255
    { 11256, "What's the situation?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11256
    { 11257, "We got us a spy on the loose." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11257
    { 11258, "CIA?" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11258
    { 11259, "Heck if I know. Can't get straight answers out of anybody around here." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11259
    { 11260, "All right! Close in!" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11260
    { 11261, "Shoot to kill!" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11261
    { 11262, "Hello... Hello, my name is... Hello, my name is Tom Goodman. Yes, I'm Tom Goodman, master spy. Hey, sugar, ever made it with a spy? The name's Tom Goodman. They call me Tom. Well, hello, there... crap! " }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11262
    { 11263, "This is the audio diary of Tom Goodman, volume 1, August 7, 1965. My spy training kit arrived in the mail today from Mr. X. It includes a UNITY field manual, a telephone monitoring device, and this tape recorder. I've decided to keep a log of my experiences for my memoirs. That way... Dang it!" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11263
    { 11264, "This is the diary of Tom Goodman, volume 2, August 14, 1965. Operation Imitation is proceeding ahead of schedule. It's only been a few weeks since I met Mr. X at that dive in Ft. Lauderdale and already I have become Tom Goodman, secret agent extraordinaire. Tomorrow, I begin Phase Two." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11264
    { 11265, "This is the diary of Tom Goodman, volume 3, August 27, 1965. I've installed my top secret spy headquarters in the basement. I call it my inner sanctum. It is what separates me from ordinary men. The entrance is carefully hidden so that enemy agents won't find it. They'll have to torture me if they want in." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11265
    { 11266, "This is the diary of Tom Goodman, volume 4, September 17, 1965. There's been an unfortunate setback. I've got the look, I've got the walk, I've got the moves, but I'm still not getting the chicks. Mr. X hasn't been helpful. I'm starting to wonder if he takes me seriously. What does he think I am, a sock puppet? Huh? Is that it, Mr. X? You think you can just stick your hand up my butt and make me dance? Tom Goodman dances for nobody." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11266
    { 11267, "Diary of Tom Goodman, volume 5, December 9, 1965. A breakthrough at last. She wasn't good-looking and she smelled like a horse, but she was woman enough for me. The last obstacle to my success as a super spy has been conquered. As of today, I am no longer a virgin. Yeeeeeeehawwwwww!" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11267
    { 11268, "Find her! Quickly!" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11268
    { 11269, "Wait here." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11269
    { 11270, "Shhh. Listen!" }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11270
    { 11271, "Wait here. I'll be back shortly." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11271
    { 11272, "You can't enter." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11272
    { 11273, "This place is not for you." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11273
    { 11274, "I'm sorry, but this area is off limits to you." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11274
    { 11275, "Employees only." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11275
    { 11276, "Go away." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11276
    { 11277, "I said, go away." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11277
    { 11278, "Psst." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11278
    { 11279, "Cate." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11279
    { 11280, "Yoo hoo." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11280
    { 11281, "Grab those Wanted posters before someone recognizes us." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11281
    { 11282, "I bring word from Kamal. He wants to meet with you as soon as possible." }, // IDS_DIALOGUE_11282
